{"name":"Ceylanite","hex":"#33431e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ceylanite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of ceylonite."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceylanite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ceylonite","blocks":[{"text":"Ceylonite and pleonaste or pleonast are dingy blue or grey-to-black varieties of spinel. Ceylonite, named for the island of Ceylon, is a ferroan spinel mineral with Mg:Fe from 3:1 and 1:1, and little or no ferric iron. Pleonaste is named from the Greek for 'abundant,' for its many crystal forms, and is distinguished chemically by low Mg:Fe ratios of approximately 1:3. It is sometimes used as a gemstone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Ceylonite%2C_calcite_7100.1.0461.jpg/330px-Ceylonite%2C_calcite_7100.1.0461.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceylonite","wikidata":"Q5065822"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Navadne podvihanke (Paxillus involutus)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Navadne_podvihanke_%28Paxillus_involutus%29.jpg/500px-Navadne_podvihanke_%28Paxillus_involutus%29.jpg","ratio":1.5548780487804879,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Navadne_podvihanke_(Paxillus_involutus).jpg","share":0.160625},{"title":"Green mangoes in tree","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Green_mangoes_in_tree.jpg/500px-Green_mangoes_in_tree.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_mangoes_in_tree.jpg","share":0.155},{"title":"Green-fee","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Green-fee.jpg/500px-Green-fee.jpg","ratio":1.5630434782608695,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green-fee.jpg","share":0.151875},{"title":"Bali, Rice fields, Rice terraces in East Bali, Indonesia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/